{"id":46767476097238,"type":"album","name":"On the Beach","artist":"Neil Young","year":1974,"weight":62,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711009.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-39fe3778-362c-4762-89fc-c03235fd8117/mbid-39fe3778-362c-4762-89fc-c03235fd8117-4477004070.jpg","label":"Reprise Records","kind":"Album","tracks":8,"country":"XE","aoty":95,"aoty_user":85,"yt":"Cby46XsFm7Y","links":{"discogs":"https://www.discogs.com/release/579392","bandcamp":"https://pereubu.bandcamp.com/album/on-the-beach-1978","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/neil-young/on-the-beach","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/f4174531-b783-3786-b75f-4fe61a8f6333","allmusic":"https://www.allmusic.com/album/mw0000049072","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/5993-neil-young-on-the-beach.php"},"desc":"Following the 1973 Time Fades Away tour, Neil Young wrote and recorded an Irish wake of a record called Tonight's the Night and went on the road drunkenly playing its songs to uncomprehending listeners and hostile reviewers. Reprise rejected the record, and Young went right back and made On the Beach, which shares some of the ragged style of its two predecessors. But where Time was embattled and Tonight mournful, On the Beach was savage and, ultimately, triumphant. \"I'm a vampire, babe,\" Young sang, and he proceeded to take bites out of various subjects: threatening the lives of the stars .","credits":{"art direction, design":["Gary Burden"],"lettering":["Rick Griffin (2)"],"photography by":["Bob Seidemann"],"sleeve notes":["Rusty Kershaw"],"written-by":["Neil Young"]}},"artist_ref":{"id":29900611348320,"name":"Neil Young","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Neil_Young_Stavernfestivalen_2016_%28220929%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[{"id":186415143977772,"type":"label","name":"Reprise Records","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":41,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"}],"genres":[{"id":185670346256268,"type":"genre","name":"rock","artist":null,"y